// @collection supplies Array's storage members and operations: count,
// capacity, @many elements, append, read, write, and the @iteration function.
//
// @equatable is written after @collection: it reads the equals that
// @collection emits, so `a = b` compares count and elements, never capacity.

@collection
@equatable
construct Array<Element> {}

// Proposed Array behavior: elements are ordered, and filtering preserves that
// order. The resulting collection is another Array<Element>.
// Array has no written members: its value is the members @collection emits.
